\newlabel{fig:paired}{{1}{8}{Per-problem economy on the 26 problems both arms prove, against problem index: notional cost, wall-clock solve time, LLM calls, and tool calls. Ultra Fleeting (dashed) tends to finish the easy shared items faster via parallel node-filling; Control~II (solid) occasionally pays a large premium on a few (\run {fatex\_069}, \run {fatex\_083}). No arm dominates the shared set}{figure.caption.2}{}}
